  "name": "Environmental Conditions Near Portlock and Albatross Banks (Gulf of Alaska) May 1972",
  "description": "The extensive oceanographic investigations in the northern North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea conducted by the Northwest Fisheries Science Center (and its predecessor, the Bureau of Commercial Fisheries Seattle Biological Laboratory) under the supervision of the American Section of the International North Pacific Fisheries Commission were terminated in summer 1971, and the activities of this group were shifted to investigations associated with the newly initiated Marine Resource, Monitoring, Assessment and Prediction program. [Reference: FAVORITE, F., W. J. INGRAHAM, Jr., and D. M. FISK. 1975. Environmental conditions near Portlock and Albatross Banks (Gulf of Alaska) May 1972. NWFC Processed Rep., 45 p. Northwest Fish. Cent., Natl. Mar. Fish. Serv., NOAA, 7600 Sand Point Way NE, Seattle, WA 98115.]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To provide environmental conditions near Portlock and Albatross Banks.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563685",
